          "lineage": "Amphizoa",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "description": "Amphizoa lecontei is a species of aquatic beetle. Adults have a body length of between 11.5 and 16 millimeters. Its elytron has a distinct carina on fifth interval. The species is found in western North America, especially in the Rocky Mountains. Its common name is \"Trout-stream beetle\". Its synonym is Amphizoa carinata.",
