          "name": "Amphizoa striata",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "lineage": "Amphizoa",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "description": "Amphizoa striata is a species of trout-stream beetle in the family Amphizoidae. It is found in North America. It is between 13 and 15 millimeters long. Its front tarsi have a well-developed groove on the posterior surface and grooves bearing a fringe of long hair-like setae. It lives in British Columbia, Oregon, and Washington.",
